    <string name="version_x">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="by_cybergah">A Cybergah project</string>
    <string name="about_voices_title">Built-in voices</string>
    <string name="about_voices_note">The models live inside the app; they are unpacked on the device the first time you use them, with no download.</string>
    <string name="about_text">Reads PDF, DOCX, EPUB and TXT documents aloud on the device, fully offline, using Piper (VITS/ONNX) voice models. The Turkish and Kurmanji voices ship inside the app.\n\nPDF pages are shown exactly as they are and the sentence being read is marked on the page. The text is decoded in pieces: reading starts as soon as the first sentence is ready and the rest is turned into speech while you listen.\n\nTriple-tap anywhere to continue reading from that point.</string>
    <string name="about_use_title">What it is good for</string>
    <string name="about_use">• Reads documents aloud for blind and low-vision users.\n• People with dyslexia or reading difficulty can follow the text by ear.\n• Long reports, assignments and books get finished on the way to work.\n• The Kurmanji voice makes listening in one\'s mother tongue possible.\n• Scanned PDFs are recognised on the device with OCR (Turkish + Kurmanji).\n• Set as the system speech engine, the Kurmanji voice works across the whole phone.\n• Everything runs offline: no internet, account or subscription.</string>

    <string name="about_speak_title">Read a text and save MP3</string>
    <string name="about_speak">Besides documents, it reads any text you type yourself. The same text can be saved as an MP3 into Downloads/Xwendevan and shared — listen in the car, in class or offline.</string>

    <string name="about_privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="about_privacy">The app never goes online; your text, documents and generated audio stay on the device. No ads, no tracking, no account. The only permissions are notifications (playback controls) and, on Android 9 and older, writing the MP3 into Downloads.</string>

    <string name="about_engine_title">Built with</string>
    <string name="about_engine">Speech engine: sherpa-onnx · ONNX Runtime · espeak-ng\nVoice models: Piper (VITS)\nMP3: jump3r (LAME)
OCR: Tesseract\nPDF text: PDFBox</string>

    <string name="about_license_title">Licence and rights</string>
    <string name="about_license">Xwendevan is free software; because of the espeak-ng component it is distributed under GPL-3.0 or later. Anyone may obtain, study and modify the source.\n\nComponent licences: sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0) · ONNX Runtime (MIT) · espeak-ng (GPL-3.0) · Piper (MIT) · PDFBox (Apache-2.0) · Material Components (Apache-2.0) · jump3r/LAME (LGPL-2.1) · Tesseract4Android (Apache-2.0) · Leptonica (BSD-2)\n\nVoice models:\n• Kurmanji — Berfin &amp; Renas: CC BY-NC 4.0 (rojanu)\n• Turkish — Murat: dfki dataset, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0\n• Turkish — Yelda, Fahrettin: Piper community models\n\nBecause of the NC (non-commercial) terms, neither the app nor the audio it produces may be sold; education, accessibility and personal use are free.</string>

    <string name="about_cybergah_title">Cybergah</string>
    <string name="about_cybergah">Cybergah is a compass for young people finding their way through the digital age: from artificial intelligence to cyber security, from software to game development. Publishing in Turkish and Kurmanji, it keeps knowledge reachable in one\'s mother tongue — because language is identity, knowledge is power, technology is the future. That is why Xwendevan exists: not merely to consume technology, but to build it.</string>
    <string name="cybergah_slogan">Your headquarters of freedom in the digital noise</string>
    <string name="cybergah_note">Xwendevan is an open project of the Cybergah community.</string>
